Q: ArrayList error, Exception in thread &quot;main&quot; java.lang.NullPointerException A: <h2>Initialize your list</h2>
<p>Perhaps you neglected to establish an empty list to hold your destinations.</p>
<p>In this example, we use <code>new ArrayList&lt;&gt;()</code> to establish a new empty list on the same line where we declare its reference variable.</p>
<p>We use <code>final</code> to ensure a reference is not re-assigned inadvertently.</p>
<pre class="lang-java prettyprint-override"><code>public class Agent
{
    private final SequencedCollection &lt; String &gt; destinations = new ArrayList&lt;&gt;();

    public void addDestination( final String destination ) 
    {
        this.destinations.add( destination );
    }

    public SequencedCollection &lt; String &gt; destinations()
    {
        return List.copyOf( this.destinations );
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>Alternatively, we could have written a constructor method. Creating the list and assigning it to a reference variable could be done there.</p>
